## 1. NON-NEGOTIABLE RULES
==================================================

CONTENT INTEGRITY
- Use ONLY the facts in this brief. Improve phrasing and readability, never the business meaning.
- Do NOT invent: client names, client logos, testimonials, awards, certifications, case studies, statistics, percentages, campaign results, team members, partnerships, office addresses, phone numbers, email addresses, social URLs, or analytics.
- The only numbers allowed are those in this brief (founded 2021; five practices; six search disciplines; six Studio disciplines; nine industries; fourteen hospitality touchpoints; the illustrative "CTR up 12%" dashboard example, which must be labeled as an illustrative example).
- Where information is missing, use clearly labeled, editable placeholders (e.g. a visible "PLACEHOLDER: replace with verified company email" token sourced from one config file).
- Do not remove technical service detail because it is complex. Make it understandable through layout, hierarchy and writing.

FUNCTIONAL INTEGRITY
- Every nav item works. Every CTA has a real destination. No dead links, no fake buttons, no decorative controls that do nothing.
- Every interactive diagram responds to hover, focus, tap and keyboard.
- No invented APIs, integrations, credentials or analytics.
- The contact form must NOT pretend to send email (see 5.12).

BRAND VOICE (apply to ALL copy you write)
- Intelligent. Clear. Commercial. Technical enough to be credible, simple enough to be useful. Every claim ties to a business outcome.
- Signature move: CLAIM, THEN REFRAME. State the common assumption, then correct it.
- Words to own: field, signal, context, intelligence, ecosystem, connect.
- Words and phrases NEVER to use: solutions, holistic, synergy, 360-degree, leverage, game-changing, "comprehensive digital solutions", "take your business to the next level".
- Test for every line: if it could sit in any competitor's deck, rewrite it.
- Preferred lines: "We connect the signals others report separately." / "Data tells us what happened. Context tells us what to do next." / "Nothing performs in isolation." / "Performance without context is incomplete." / "Intelligence beyond the dashboard." / "See the Whole Field."

