## 3. DESIGN SYSTEM
==================================================

3.1 COLOR TOKENS (define once as CSS variables and Tailwind theme extensions; never hard-code hex elsewhere)
- --violet: #B34FFF   --magenta: #E23389
- --off-white: #F4F1EA   --near-black: #010102   --electric-blue: #0057FF
- Balance across the site: ~70% off-white surfaces, ~15% near-black, ~15% electric blue. Violet and magenta are used for gradients, highlights, key words and the dot, not as large flat fills. Dark gradient sections are feature moments (hero, intelligence framework, final CTA, hospitality hero), not the default.
- Electric Blue sparingly: link underlines, focus rings, active states, small accents, diagram highlights.
- Derived tints (opacity or color-mix of the above) are allowed for borders and muted text. Do not introduce any unrelated hues. No random neon.
- SIGNATURE GRADIENT MESH (dark-centre): base #010102; radial layers: bottom-left #B34FFF at full strength fading to transparent toward the centre, bottom-right #E23389 at full strength fading toward the centre, top-left and top-right pure #010102. The centre stays dark for depth and text contrast. Build as layered radial-gradients plus a very subtle noise overlay. Optional, very slow gradient drift (CSS only, GPU-friendly, disabled under reduced motion).
- GRADIENT TEXT: violet → magenta fill, for hero moments and key headline words only. Never for running text.
- Contrast: all text must meet WCAG AA (4.5:1 body, 3:1 large). Verify violet or magenta text on off-white and on near-black; if a pair fails, use near-black or off-white text with a gradient accent element instead.

3.2 TYPOGRAPHY
- Typeface: Sora ONLY (Google Fonts), weights 300, 400, 600, 700, 800. Preload critical weights, font-display: swap, with a system sans-serif fallback stack that has similar metrics.
- Type scale (desktop reference, use fluid clamp() so it scales down): Heading 80px Sora ExtraBold · Subheading 30px Sora SemiBold in CAPITALS (e.g. SEE THE WHOLE FIELD) · Body 20px Sora Regular. Add intermediate sizes for h3 to h6, captions and UI labels. On mobile, the 80px heading becomes roughly 40–48px.
- Headlines: bold, forward-leaning (use italic or a skewX transform on display headings only, never on body text or long paragraphs). Tight tracking on display, comfortable line-height (1.5–1.7) on body.
- Max line length ~68 characters for body copy.
- NEVER type the logo in Sora. The logo is custom artwork (see 3.3).

3.3 LOGO SYSTEM (PLACEHOLDER MODE)
The real logo has: the Wordmark "Digital Field." (stacked, heavy forward-leaning italic custom artwork) and the Icon "DF." (an integrated italic numeral 1, a sharp forward-leaning D that shares its top stroke with the F, and a magenta block "dot" at the foot of the F). Lockups: Standard (upright divider between icon and wordmark) and Italic (divider follows the slant).
- The real files are NOT available. Create ONE reusable <Logo /> component with variants: "wordmark", "icon", "lockup-standard", "lockup-italic", and with theme variants for light and dark backgrounds.
- Each variant must render a clearly labeled PLACEHOLDER (e.g. a neutral outlined block with the small text "LOGO PLACEHOLDER") that is obviously temporary, plus a single config path per variant (e.g. /src/assets/brand/logo-lockup.svg) so the client can drop in official SVGs and everything updates. Do NOT redraw, approximate or retype the icon, 1, D, F or dot.
- Rules to encode in a code comment and a /brand-guidelines.md in the repo: clear space = 1X on all sides where X = the size of the dot; never stretch, squash, recolor outside the approved palette, add or remove elements, fade, add shadows, outlines or glows, tilt or rotate; below legible size switch wordmark to icon.
- Use the wordmark in header, footer, proposals and sign-offs; use the icon for favicon (placeholder), mobile header at small sizes, section markers and watermarks.

3.4 GRAPHIC LANGUAGE
- ONE ANGLE: every angled element (dividers, shapes, pattern, clip-paths, underlines, section edges) uses the same forward slant. Define it once as a token (e.g. --slant: -12deg; pick a single value and reuse it) so the whole identity moves in one direction.
- DF. PATTERN: a repeating pattern of forward-slanted parallelogram or bar modules. Official artwork is not available, so build a tasteful abstract slanted-geometry pattern as a swappable <BrandPattern /> component (SVG), documented as a placeholder for the official pattern. Use it for texture on dark or gradient surfaces with enough empty space for content. Keep it legible and subtle.
- TRIDI MARK: an inverted triangle emblem (TRI = triangle, DI = digital) built from the icon's letterforms. Official art is unavailable: create a swappable <TridiMark /> placeholder component using a plain inverted-triangle geometric motif, labeled in code as a placeholder, used only as a secondary emblem on dark and gradient surfaces, never as a logo replacement.
- 3D DF. ICON: used for the hero and launch moments. Do not build a fake 3D logo. Build the hero visual as an abstract glossy 3D-feeling composition (layered slanted glass planes, glossy gradient forms with violet and magenta glow, subtle depth parallax) using CSS 3D transforms and SVG, with a clearly marked <Hero3DSlot /> where the official 3D icon render (PNG, WebM or GLB) can be dropped in. Avoid heavy 3D libraries unless justified; if Three.js is used it must be lazy-loaded, capped for performance, and have a static fallback.
- GLASSMORPHISM: translucent panels, backdrop-blur, 1px light borders, only on dark gradient surfaces. Never on off-white sections.
- LAYOUTS: use L-shape and T-shape compositions (a bold heading anchoring an edge with content flowing along an axis), split-screen, editorial asymmetry, full-bleed bands, a bento grid (max two uses), process or timeline diagrams, big-type statement sections. Vary layouts from section to section; avoid repeating identical card grids.
- Do not overcrowd with decoration. One hero visual per section at most.

3.5 PHOTOGRAPHY AND IMAGERY
- Direction: authentic, editorial; real people, creative collaboration, modern hospitality and digital experiences; natural expressions, confident compositions, considered lighting. Do: real settings, natural expression. Don't: stiff staged poses, handshake or generic stock clichés, flat or careless lighting.
- No approved photography is supplied. Build a reusable <ImageSlot /> component: fixed aspect ratio (prevents layout shift), brand-gradient or pattern fill, a visible small "PHOTO PLACEHOLDER: [shot description]" label, an editable alt text field in data, and a single place to set the real image src (with width and height, loading="lazy", srcset or sizes ready). The shot description should state the desired photo (e.g. "Creative professionals collaborating in a real working environment, natural light").
- Do NOT hotlink random stock photos. Do NOT use fabricated "client" imagery.
- BRAND CHARACTERS Di & Fi: two AI-generated brand characters named after Digital and Field, each with a defined look. No reference images are supplied, so do NOT invent their appearance. Create an optional <CharacterSlot name="Di" | "Fi" /> placeholder that renders nothing visible in production unless images are configured, and note the AI-disclosure requirement ("label AI-generated imagery wherever disclosure is required").

3.6 SIGNATURE POSTER / SOCIAL LAYOUT (also used for the Open Graph image spec)
Bold headline in Sora capitals (e.g. SEE THE WHOLE FIELD, SHAPE THE FUTURE, CHOOSE TO BE DIFFERENT); wordmark bottom-left; DIGITALFIELD.CO bottom-right; dark gradient background; one hero visual.

3.7 MOTION PRINCIPLES
Premium, controlled, purposeful. Allowed: smooth route transitions (short fade and slight slide on the slant axis), subtle entrance reveals, scroll-triggered reveals and storytelling, interactive diagrams, refined hover states (underline slants, magnetic-free), slow animated gradient details, sophisticated headline reveals (mask or line-by-line), subtle parallax, carefully limited 3D tilt. Forbidden: bouncing, constant spinning, distracting backgrounds, custom cursor effects, many simultaneous animations, heavy animation libraries or assets, anything harming readability. ALL motion must honour prefers-reduced-motion (swap to instant or simple fades, disable parallax, drift and 3D tilt). Animate only transform and opacity where possible.

