## 7. RESPONSIVE, ACCESSIBILITY, SEO, PERFORMANCE
==================================================

RESPONSIVE (large desktop ≥1440, laptop ~1280, tablet ~768, mobile ~375). Recompose, don't just shrink: stacked hero with smaller but still bold headline; mobile nav with full-screen menu; diagrams switch to vertical or step-based versions; service lists use accordions on mobile; forms single-column with large tap targets (≥44px); footer reorganizes into stacked groups; no horizontal scroll at any width; test at 320px.

ACCESSIBILITY (WCAG 2.2 AA): semantic landmarks (header, nav, main, footer); one h1 per page and logical heading order; skip-to-content link; visible focus rings (Electric Blue); full keyboard operability including all diagrams, menu, tabs and accordions; correct ARIA for tabs, accordions, dialogs and live regions; sufficient contrast; prefers-reduced-motion support; do not rely on color alone; form labels and errors; meaningful alt text (decorative visuals get alt="" or aria-hidden); touch-target size; no autoplaying motion that cannot be paused beyond reduced-motion handling.

SEO: semantic HTML; unique <title> (≤60 chars) and meta description (≤155 chars) per route via a usePageMeta hook/config; Open Graph and Twitter tags per route with a placeholder og:image; canonical tag per route (using a placeholder base URL from config); descriptive alt text; internal linking between related pages; clean route names; sitemap.xml and robots.txt; JSON-LD: Organization (name, foundingDate 2021, founder Islam Helal, address locality Dubai, country AE; omit url, phone, email and sameAs unless config values are real) and Service / ItemList structured data for the five practices and the six search disciplines, BreadcrumbList on deeper pages, FAQ-style content only if real Q&A exists (do not invent). Keep the terminology SEO, AEO, AIO, GEO, GAIO and AXO intact in headings and text. Note in the README that a client-side SPA has SEO limitations and recommend prerendering or SSR (e.g. Vite SSG or migrating to a framework with SSR) before launch; implement what is possible now.

PERFORMANCE: route-level code splitting; lazy-load below-the-fold sections and diagrams; ImageSlot with fixed aspect ratios, lazy loading, srcset/sizes and modern formats ready; minimal dependencies; animate transform/opacity only; pause offscreen animations; hero visual loads fast with a static fallback; preload critical Sora weights; avoid layout shift (CLS < 0.1 target), keep LCP fast (< 2.5s target) and INP responsive; no heavy video or large assets bundled; respect Save-Data/reduced-motion where practical.

